{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id1356588728"}, "name":{"label":"LAKnight5386"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-01-05T19:04:00-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.8.5"}, "id":{"label":"12150297788"}, "title":{"label":"Promising but not perfect."}, "content":{"label":"I’ve purchased seeing the initial promises it made and the concept of time blocking with timer and purchased a lifetime subscription. However, as a person that sometimes is on their computer, phone and watch, it doesn’t seem to sync changes properly across all platforms creating chaos. When I make a change on the schedule on the computer, it won’t sync with the app on the phone and then the watch too. The time taken to clean up or get it to work, it’s easier to just make a mental note and carry on with the day. I’m hoping this issue is resolved and am willing to work with the developing team if needed as I believe in the potential of this app (hence the lifetime subscription).", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=1499198946&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id117991186"}, "name":{"label":"Jason_C_8_nickname"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-01-05T10:23:10-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.8.5"}, "id":{"label":"12148859193"}, "title":{"label":"Great but..."}, "content":{"label":"I never write reviews but I felt the need to for this app. It's great, I love it. If a reader is debating whether or not to give it a try, you should, design, interface, intuitiveness, features, etc, it's solid.\n\nThat being said, there are a few features that would really put it over the top and for me, would justify the annual subscription.\n1) I sometimes like to move tasks around the day by dragging them - which the app does perfectly. However it's really difficult to drop it precisely where i want (example at the start time I want) because of the collapsible nature of the schedule. Ideally the day's layout would expand fully when modifying the schedule\n2) Would be great if i could drag multiple tasks at the same time, say I'm running late and want to push everything back by 30min, currently it seems the only way to do this is one by one which is a bit tedious\n3) Would also be great if i could drag the upper/lower edge of the task bubble on the planner view to make it start earlier or finish later without moving the bubble entirely. Currently i would have to open the task and edit it. not a big deal but something i'd appreciate\n\non a side note, the macOS version doesn't seem to be showing the task i just created from the macOS version itself, even though it syncs and is visible on my ios version. Admittedly, i'm on macOS 14.4 so maybe i just need to update to the latest version to fix this.\n\nHope the feedback might be useful to the devs! Otherwise, love the app, keep it up!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=1499198946&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
